// BT-3590 (ADR 0127 §3/§10): an Actor class's `uses:` provision must reach
// compiled Core Erlang output through the existing gen_server generator
// unchanged, including a provision that self-sends another of the class's
// own (non-provided) methods across the actor state boundary.
//
// See `trait_flattened_value_user/main.bt`'s header comment for why this
// single-file fixture (protocol + class together) is not itself a
// legal package layout, and why its `_semantic` snapshot's "class and a
// protocol cannot be in the same file" diagnostic is expected.

Protocol define: Greetable
  greet -> String => self greeting

Actor subclass: Greeter
  uses: Greetable
  state: greetingCount = 0

  greeting -> String => "hi"

  bump => self.greetingCount := self.greetingCount + 1
